    "review": "Official C145 schematic and Tab5 manual give one shared P4/expander/audio/SD wiring map for all three published panel assemblies. The pinned BSP supplies distinct panel timings/init and GPIO23 handling, selected by the touch controller. Unknown panel firmware fails closed. No factory-binary pin inference used. INA226 0x41/5 mOhm shunt, BMI270 0x68 and RX8130CE 0x32 use the same published shared I2C1 map; identity and configuration readback precede telemetry. The RTC backup control matches the fitted rechargeable supply. Charger/rail controls stay excluded. USB-A J10 and its masked 0x44/P3 enable are additionally scoped by the pinned USB-controller schematic/BSP review. USB-C Serial/JTAG remains independent. User subsequently approved the exact C6 radio scope and requested battery charging. These narrowly scoped authorizations extend the prior 0.44 scope.",
